        <p>Bel(</p>
        <p>Serious Fire at Vale Royal. A serious fire occurred at Vale Royal, near North- wich, Cheshire, the seat of Lord Delamere on Tues- day night. About ten o'clock the extensive stab- ling connscted with the historic hall was discovered to be in flames and mei•sages were despatcned for the North wich and Winsford Brigades, which were speedily in attendance. (hey found the buildings largely composed of oak, in flames. A plentiful supply of water was found and turned in volume, on the burning mass. Tee stabling was practically destroyed, but the adjacent buildings were saved. Valuable horses and carriages were removed to safe quarters. The damags is very considerable.</p>
