      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-04-26_WidnesExaminer_art0033" n="art0033">
        <head>PURGATIVES &amp; STIMULANTS.</head>
        <p>PURGATIVES &amp; STIMULANTS.</p>
        <p>Purgatives are misused by many people much in the same way that Stimulants are abused by others: namely, to tide them over a difficulty or an ailment, instead of meeting it squarely. If you are Bilious, or have Indigestion and Headache, a purgative will seem to do you good- though of course it weakens: but nothing is cured. The stomach is irritated and empties itself: that is all that happens: the cause remains, namely, inability of the system to assimilate its food. It would be far less foolish to use an emetic: but neither would do any real good.</p>
        <p>Dr. Williams' Pink Pills</p>
        <p>for Pale People,</p>
        <p>on the contrary, cure you by giving fresh strength, enabling the stomach and all the organs to do their work: they increase and enrich the blood Hence they cure permanently--whether it be Biliousness and Indigestion, or Anxmia, Rheumatism, or Weakness in any form. Similarly, if you think you cannot work well without stimulants, which only give temporary strength, tone• yourself up by a short course of Dr. Williams' Pink Pills they</p>
