        <head>PERMANENTLY STRENGTHEN.</head>
        <p>PERMANENTLY STRENGTHEN.</p>
        <p>"ALMOST helpless, and a wreck of her former self,- fitly described, not long ago, the state of Mrs. Agnes Brown, of 14, Hopeton Street, Gourock, Renfrewshire. She stated to a Greenock Herald reporter : I was always ailing and out of sorts, and the feeling upset me so altog,ether, that I was quite unfit for any work in my home. My appetite left me, and food remained undigested in the system, causing me much distress through flatulency. I had severe pains in the stomach after taking any food, and everything gave -me a nausea, even to look at it. The trouble became so serious that life was an utter misery. I was treated by several doctors, and took a quantity of medicine, but der i ved no perceptible good. Then a friend recommended me to try Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People. I was told that these pills had proved most valuable to many 'others, and I gladly turned to a remedythat promised so well. I tried the rills, and soon found that I was suffering less Pain. One box gave me great relief, and by continuing regularly with Dr. Williams' Pink Pills my strength came back, and I able to derive nourishment from food. I can now eat and enjoy my food, without dreading a great deal of pain and discomfort." Mrs. Brown has a little daughter, thirteen years of age, who was a martyr to biliousries and indigestion. Dr. Williams' Pink Pills were administered according to directions, and now she is quite well and free from biliousness.</p>
