        <p>The following verses are given not as a sample of what can be done in the competition, but to show the rhythm of the verses to any who may be un- acquainted with them.</p>
        <p>Five verses should end with "My Mother" and one with "Why Boots," or some similarly suitable syllables.</p>
        <p>Who, when the Spring came would dltect Her efforts, e'en by pa unchecked, Boots Ota us to use with grand effect ? My mother</p>
        <p>Whose Stains do most our floors adorn? Whose Gold Paint hails the smiling morn? Whose Polish turns all dirt to scorn? Why Boots I</p>
