      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-04-26_WidnesExaminer_art0041" n="art0041">
        <head>CONDITIONS.</head>
        <p>CONDITIONS.</p>
        <p>What we consider the beet and cleverest verses will be awarded prizes as above in their respective order of merit. The verses must be sent, post paid, on or be- fore 30th May, 1901. and accompanied by a receipt for something need for spring cleani g, bought at any of the branches of BOOTS. Cash Chemists. You will get a receipt for everything you buy at the shops Of BOOTS, Cash Chemists.</p>
        <p>The verses to become the property of BOOTS, Cash Chemists, for publication if desired. but the sender's name will not be published without permiuion.</p>
        <p>Two or more sets of verses will be accepted from one sender, but each set must be accompanied by a separate receipt.</p>
        <p>Prizes will not be awarded to employees of the arm.</p>
        <p>The decision of the Manager of the competition must be accepted as final.</p>
        <p>• WRITE PLAINLY AND GIVE YOUR ADDRESS. ADDRESS YOUR LETTER TO— "MV MOTHER," Vico BOOTS, CASH CHEMISTS, NOTTINGHAM.</p>
      </div>
