      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-04-26_WidnesExaminer_art0062" n="art0062">
        <head>LANDMARK ALREADY.</head>
        <p>A LANDMARK ALREADY.</p>
        <p>The year 1901 has already become a landnr-_rk in the history of the United Kingdom, and sorrow h marked with unwonted universality the wbo!e of the nations of the Earth. How true is it, that grief and 01 Won are the common lot of al, and that suffering co. ies to all Irma and women alike, the great and the low y, in the palace and in the cottage ; but in sickness there is the consolation that suffering may be assuaged. strength increased, and health—generally speaking—r,stored by attention to the dictates of Nature, and the •mlistment in man's service of the bountilul goodness tha t abounds in the fertilty of the earth, the gifts of a beneficent pro- , widence. The most striking instance of the g.athering in of these benefits for humor.i suffering is found in Gwilyno I Evans' (:asinine Bitters, which comprises a scientific I compounding of the virtues to be derived from Sarsaprr- lila, Gentian, Burdock, Lavender, Dandelion, Saffron, end Quinine: an array of health giving tonic properties not to be surpassed, even in Nature's Garnery of Good- ness. This reviving, invigorsting,strengthetii.g remedy, when other attempts to cure have failed, often brings quick relief to sufferets from weakness of boe 7, and un. strung nerves, indigestion, poor blood,depre‘ged spirits, and it increases the joy of life to all. It well may be termed " Nature's Great Tonic." -</p>
