      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-04-26_WidnesExaminer_art0085" n="art0085">
        <p>LATEST NaWS.</p>
        <p>The Miners' Federation and the Coal Tax. ITheM e F=?.deration havl passed a resolution protesting, a;,-ainst the coal tax on the ground that it is r.con,m,e ally unsound and highly dangerous to th.ir p-oitior as wage earners. THE WAR.</p>
        <p>LATEST TELEGRAMS. DISASTER IN NORTH TRANSVAAL.</p>
        <p>British Force Ambushed Major Twyford Shot. PRETORIA, APRIL, 23RD. Maj )1. Twyford and a mall escort, while proceed- ing to Lydenburg, from Machadodorp to join the Royal Scots (Lothian Regiment) fell into an ambush near Badfontein. The sc•-ue of the di3aser was in a valley near the C rre^clll," R:ver. The men made a gallant resistance and refu9nd to surrender. Eventually Major Twyford was shot and the men overpowered.</p>
