      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-04-26_WidnesExaminer_art0093" n="art0093">
        <head>LOCAL PARISH COUNCIL MEETINGS.</head>
        <p>LOCAL PARISH COUNCIL MEETINGS.</p>
        <p>Weston.</p>
        <p>The first meeting of the newly-elected Council was held at the Cnurch Scho Is, Weston, on Friday evening. Fhere were Dr lie .t :—Messrs J Ordliths, Jarnos Tudor. G Whitby, H 8 Bamber, L Rosenberg, A G Guest, H GarnPr, Jsmes Basnett, S Savage, J E C Bankes, and Jam a Collier (clerk) —Mr ruder proposed that the Rev Canon Maitland Woid b. the chairman for the ensuing year —Mr R )senberg seconded, and the motion W 45 carried unanimously.—ln the absence at the vicar Mr Guest was anpointed cAzairman for the evening, on the motion of Mr Tudor. sloon tod by Mr Qarn r.</p>
        <p>THE REPAIR OF THE FOOTPATH, LEADING TO RUNCORN.</p>
        <p>Mr Collier, the c erk, stated that he wrote to Mr C L. Evans with reference to the goo,tion of repairing the footpt,th across the field+, lealing to Runcorn, and he received the following rPplr ;—"What is it your Council want about the botpath ? If they will send a plan I will consider the matter." In reply to a second lettr'r frana the clerk, Mr Evans wrote under date February 2nd, 1901 :—" With regard to the footpath the public have merely a right of way over the land. The path could la, ploughed up if the tenant 'bought fl*. I will call and see you neat time tam in Weston." The clerk said he had not 9900 Mr Evans at present. The Chairman : Could they plough it up ? Toe Clerk : Yes. Mr Tu lor : Yes, but they would never attempt to plough that rock up. (I. tughter.)</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-04-26_WidnesExaminer_art0094" n="art0094">
        <head>APPOINTMENT OF oisnseEns</head>
        <p>APPOINTMENT OF oisnseEns</p>
        <p>On the motion at Mr L R.seahure, seconded by Mr Whitby, Messrs fhomis Ford, senior, and A G Guest were re-elec'ed overseers.</p>
        <p>FINANCIAL.</p>
        <p>NO PRECEPT REQUIRED The Clerk ssid there waa an account of Ss for use of schnot room for ihs parish meeting, and another of 118. returning Mike 's fee for conducting the uncontested election of parish councillors. It was resolved that the accounts be paid. The Clerk said he was very pleased to inform the Council that they would not need to issue a precept up- on the °veneers for the next six months. This time lasr year they were indebted to the treasurer to the extent of 3 71. but at the 31st March last they had a balance in band of £2 131 41. There wee the two accounts Fist passed, amounting to 161 to come out of that sum, and the balance was likely to meet all their liabilities for the next six months. If they found they needed more money, they could issue a precept later on. He did not think they would need any, TUE COUNCIL MEETINGS.</p>
        <p>It CVAIR CllCidAd hit th • m,etings of the Council should be Ir3ld alternately at Weston and Weston Point.</p>
