      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-04-26_WidnesExaminer_art0095" n="art0095">
        <head>Dutton.</head>
        <p>Dutton.</p>
        <p>The annual meeting of tie Parish Council and the first for the newly e'ected members, was held in ths Board tactioel ol Thursday last week Mr Potta proposed, and Mr Baxter seconded, that Mr Rob In Fowles be re- elected chairman of the Council. Mr Fowles proposed Mr BAK' er, and Mr Itichardson seconded. Mr Ssokes gave his casting vote in faveur of Mr Fowles, wh I was declared duly elected. Mr Fowles then took the chair, ond thanked the members for basing re-elected him. Mr Fax', r was unanimously elected vice-chairman. It was propo,ej by Mr Baxter, and seconded by Mr Rich- ard/ion, that Mr Potts be. the first overseer, and Mr ch rdsla, on the pro loszioci of Mr Powles. second, d by M, Samuel Kiosey. Was appointed the secood. the Clerk then read tho overseers' statement of accounts for the han-year e .ding 25-1 March, from whichi it ap- peared that rho balance n han on Septembe* 29-b last -.cam £3 34 10d; rates, £5"17 1. 21; total, £530 5;. Ex- penditure—County police. £135, ; poor, £123 ; School Bari, £B7; svi arr. £32 ; high ay. £142; overseers' experses, £l5 19, 34; total, £534 19s 31, leaving a balance of £455. 91 in the bank. The sum of lla was passed for payment to Mr U F Aftron, as returning offic?r in the uncotiteel Parish Council Election. `</p>
